            "htmlContent": "\u003csection class\u003d\"article-section article-section__abstract\" lang\u003d\"en\" data-lang\u003d\"en\" id\u003d\"section-1-en\"\u003e\n   \u003ch3 class\u003d\"article-section__header main abstractlang_en main\"\u003eAbstract\u003c/h3\u003e\n   \u003cdiv class\u003d\"article-section__content en main\"\u003e\n      \n      \n      \u003cdiv class\u003d\"article-section__content\" id\u003d\"assep001-sec-0001\"\u003e\n         \n         \u003cp\u003eThis chapter covers the basic aspects of liquid chromatography such as retention models,\n            kinetics, band broadening, the plate height concept, and the dependence of separation\n            performance on flow rate. Together, this will form a basis to understand how to predict\n            and improve separation performance and resolution for different types of HPLC systems. We conclude the chapter with today\u0027s trends in liquid chromatography and\n            explain how these trends are linked to the basic aspects covered earlier.\n         \u003c/p\u003e\n         \n      \u003c/div\u003e\n      \n   \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/section\u003e",
